# Storage discovery (LWS 1.0 core sections 6 and 9.1).
"@context":
  - ../context.jsonld
  - ../touchstone.jsonld
id: "#manifest"
type: Manifest
label: "LWS 1.0 core: storage discovery"
comment: >-
  How a client holding any resource URI finds the storage it belongs to, and what the
  storage description says about it. The 21 August 2026 draft replaced the
  rel="storageDescription" link with rel="https://www.w3.org/ns/lws#storage" pointing at
  the canonical storage URI, which itself serves the description as application/lws+cid.
specification:
  - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20260921/
entries:

  - id: "#discovery-get-links-storageDescription"
    type: ValidationTest
    name: discovery-get-links-storageDescription
    label: GET and HEAD of a container link to the storage it belongs to
    comment: >-
      A client that lands on any resource finds its storage through this relation, so it
      must be on every GET and HEAD response. The name is lws-test-suite's; the relation it
      asserts is the current draft's lws#storage, not the storageDescription relation the
      name recalls.
    status: Proposed
    level: MUST
    source:
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20260921/#storage-description-binding
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20260921/#metadata
    traits: [Get, Head, Discovery, Container]
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/storage-description-link-header
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/link-storage-on-responses
    mirrors: lws10/manifest.jsonld#discovery-get-links-storageDescription
    supersedes: [core/storage-description-discovery]
    steps:
      - label: GET of the test container links to its storage
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${test.container}"
          accept: application/lws+json
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          linkHeaders:
            - rel: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws#storage
              capture: storageLink
      - label: HEAD carries the same link, since a client may never fetch a body
        request:
          method: HEAD
          url: "${test.container}"
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          linkHeaders:
            - rel: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws#storage
              href: "${storageLink}"

  - id: "#discovery-link-storage-on-data-resource"
    type: ValidationTest
    name: discovery-link-storage-on-data-resource
    label: GET and HEAD of a data resource link to the same storage as its container
    comment: >-
      The storage link is required on responses for all storage resources, not only
      containers, and a data resource must name the same storage its container does.
    status: Proposed
    level: MUST
    source:
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20260921/#storage-description-binding
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20260921/#metadata
    traits: [Get, Head, Discovery, DataResource]
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/storage-description-link-header
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/link-storage-on-responses
    prereqs:
      hierarchy:
        - dataResource: created
          contentType: text/plain
          body: storage link check
    steps:
      - label: GET of the data resource links to the container's storage
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${created}"
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          linkHeaders:
            - rel: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws#storage
              href: "${storage}"
      - label: and so does HEAD
        request:
          method: HEAD
          url: "${created}"
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          linkHeaders:
            - rel: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws#storage
              href: "${storage}"

  - id: "#discovery-storage-description"
    type: ValidationTest
    name: discovery-storage-description
    label: The storage URI serves a controlled identifier document describing the storage
    comment: >-
      Follows the storage link rather than a path it assumed. The description is an
      application/lws+cid document whose @context array starts with the CID and LWS
      contexts, whose id is the storage URI, whose type includes Storage, and whose
      services include a StorageRoot. Services are matched by content, not position.
    status: Proposed
    level: MUST
    source:
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20260921/#storage-description-binding
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20260921/#storage-description-data-model
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20260921/#storage-description-representation
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20260921/#storage-description-services
    traits: [Get, Discovery, StorageDescription]
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/storage-uri-returns-lws-cid-document
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/storage-description-lws-cid
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/lws-cid-media-type-storage-description
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/storage-description-id-required
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/storage-description-type-storage
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/storage-service-property
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/storage-service-type-required
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/storage-service-endpoint-required
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/storage-description-storageroot-service
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/storage-capability-type-required
    mirrors: lws10/manifest.jsonld#discovery-storage-description
    supersedes: [core/storage-description-discovery]
    request:
      method: GET
      url: "${storage}"
      accept: application/lws+cid
    response:
      statusCode: 200
      contentType: application/lws+cid
      json:
        - pointer: /@context
          jsonType: array
        - pointer: /@context/0
          equals: https://www.w3.org/ns/cid/v1
        - pointer: /@context/1
          equals: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws/v1
        - pointer: /id
          equalsIri: "${storage}"
        - pointer: /type
          hasValue: Storage
        - pointer: /service
          jsonType: array
        - pointer: /service
          every:
            - pointer: /type
              exists: true
            - pointer: /serviceEndpoint
              jsonType: string
        - pointer: /service
          some:
            - pointer: /type
              hasValue: StorageRoot
        - pointer: /capability
          optional: true
          every:
            - pointer: /type
              exists: true

  - id: "#discovery-storage-description-default-media-type"
    type: ValidationTest
    name: discovery-storage-description-default-media-type
    label: Without content negotiation the storage URI answers application/lws+cid
    comment: >-
      The media type is required unless content negotiation asks for another, so a
      request that negotiates nothing must receive application/lws+cid.
    status: Proposed
    level: MUST
    source:
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20260921/#storage-description-binding
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20260921/#lws-media-type-0
    traits: [Get, Discovery, StorageDescription]
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/storage-uri-returns-lws-cid-document
    request:
      method: GET
      url: "${storage}"
    response:
      statusCode: 200
      contentType: application/lws+cid

  - id: "#discovery-unauthorized-response-headers"
    type: NegativeTest
    name: discovery-unauthorized-response-headers
    label: A 401 from a protected resource links to the storage
    comment: >-
      Lets a client that is refused learn where the storage description is without a
      hard-coded path. The draft is inconsistent on the level: section 6.1.2 requires
      the link on all GET and HEAD responses, while the section 9.2 notes say servers
      SHOULD include it on 401 responses. This takes the weaker reading, so a server is
      not failed for what may turn out to be optional; the 401 challenge itself is a MUST
      and is tested by getContainer-private-unauthorized.
    status: Proposed
    level: SHOULD
    source:
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20260921/#create-resource
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20260921/#storage-description-binding
    traits: [Get, Discovery, Private, Authn]
    requires: [Authentication]
    as: anonymous
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/create-401-storage-link
    mirrors: lws10/manifest.jsonld#discovery-unauthorized-response-headers
    note: >-
      lws-test-suite's version also asserted the challenge (a MUST) and used
      rel="storageDescription" with a /storage_1/metadata target; the challenge moved to
      getContainer-private-unauthorized and the relation to lws#storage.
    request:
      method: GET
      url: "${test.container}"
    response:
      statusCode: 401
      linkHeaders:
        - rel: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws#storage
          href: "${storage}"
